      {
        "Id": "3f1618864ec248e98540217a274a5e05",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE  -  draw a Room or Area named STAIR (STAIR 1, STAIR CORE ...) on each floor, Run\nA concrete dog-leg stair is fitted inside (straight if the room is narrow): landing on the far wall, start at the door side.\nRiser = real floor-to-floor height / risers (never above Max riser), tread 300 - any number of levels, any heights.\nMoved / resized the room? Run again - only changed stairs are rebuilt. Room deleted = its stair removed.",
        "DescriptionText": null,
